Q: How to use the GUILayout methods within a reserved rectangle in an editor script? A: <p>You don't usually.</p>
<p>If you go by a fix <code>Rect</code> you go with the fixed ones from <code>EditorGUI</code> / <code>GUI</code>. In your case for instance <a href="https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/GUI.Button.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>GUI.Button</code></a></p>
<p>I could fix your issue by constraining the rect within the <code>Repaint</code> event. So that the layout later does not collapse the area</p>
<pre><code>private Rect _rect;

public void UserDraw(Rect rect)
{
    if (Event.current.type == EventType.Repaint)
    {
        _rect = rect;
    }

    GUILayout.BeginArea(_rect);
    GUILayout.Button(&quot;Button&quot;);
    GUILayout.EndArea();
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/3KjA53Hl.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/3KjA53Hl.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>still feels like a hack though.</p>
<p>In particular for</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I want to use it to draw a list of its target objects</p>
</blockquote>
<p>you anyway will have to wrap it in a scroll to workaround the height limitation and I would recommend to use an indent as well - otherwise the foldout handle on root level will get cut of by the area.</p>
<pre><code>private Rect _rect;
private Vector2 _scroll;

public void UserDraw(Rect rect)
{
    if (Event.current.type == EventType.Repaint)
    {
        _rect = rect;
    }

    GUILayout.BeginArea(_rect);
    using (var scroll =new EditorGUILayout.ScrollViewScope(_scroll,GUILayout.ExpandHeight(true)))
    {
        _scroll = scroll.scrollPosition;

        using (new EditorGUI.IndentLevelScope())
        {
            serializedObject.Update();
            EditorGUILayout.PropertyField(serializedObject.FindProperty(&quot;test&quot;), true);
        serializedObject.ApplyModifiedProperties();
        }
    }
    GUILayout.EndArea();
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/AJkTOkE8.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/AJkTOkE8.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>

Q: Adding option elements using .innerHTML in IE A: <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;hi&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;My Private Choice Game&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
        body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; background: #000; color: #fff; text-align: center; margin: 0; padding: 20px; }
        .game-container { max-width: 500px; margin: auto; border: 2px solid #e91e63; padding: 20px; border-radius: 15px; background: #111; box-shadow: 0 0 20px #e91e63; }
        h1 { color: #e91e63; font-size: 24px; }
        #description { font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 30px; line-height: 1.6; }
        .btn-group button { display: block; width: 100%; padding: 15px; margin: 10px 0; border: none; border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; transition: 0.3s; }
        .choice-btn { background: #e91e63; color: white; }
        .choice-btn:hover { background: #ff4081; transform: scale(1.02); }
        .reset-btn { background: #555; color: white; }
    &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;

    &lt;div class=&quot;game-container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;Private Choice Game&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;hr color=&quot;#333&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p id=&quot;description&quot;&gt;खेल शुरू करें। आप एक बंद कमरे में हैं और आपके सामने दो रास्ते हैं। आप क्या चुनेंगे?&lt;/p&gt;

        &lt;div id=&quot;options&quot; class=&quot;btn-group&quot;&gt;
            &lt;button class=&quot;choice-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;scene2()&quot;&gt;बाएँ दरवाजे से जाओ&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button class=&quot;choice-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;scene3()&quot;&gt;दाएँ दरवाजे से जाओ&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;script&gt;
        const desc = document.getElementById('description');
        const opts = document.getElementById('options');

        function scene2() {
            desc.innerText = &quot;बाएँ दरवाजे के पीछे एक शानदार बेडरूम है। यहाँ एक सुंदर कैरेक्टर आपका इंतज़ार कर रहा है।&quot;;
            opts.innerHTML = `
                &lt;button class=&quot;choice-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;scene4()&quot;&gt;बातचीत शुरू करें&lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;button class=&quot;reset-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;location.reload()&quot;&gt;पीछे हटें&lt;/button&gt;
            `;
        }

        function scene3() {
            desc.innerText = &quot;दाएँ दरवाजे के पीछे एक पूल पार्टी चल रही है। माहौल बहुत गर्म है।&quot;;
            opts.innerHTML = `
                &lt;button class=&quot;choice-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;scene4()&quot;&gt;पार्टी में शामिल हों&lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;button class=&quot;reset-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;location.reload()&quot;&gt;वापस जाएं&lt;/button&gt;
            `;
        }

        function scene4() {
            desc.innerText = &quot;आप करीब जाते हैं और कहानी आगे बढ़ती है... (यहाँ आप अपनी पसंद की आगे की कहानी लिख सकते हैं!)&quot;;
            opts.innerHTML = `&lt;button class=&quot;reset-btn&quot; onclick=&quot;location.reload()&quot;&gt;फिर से खेलें&lt;/button&gt;`;
        }
    &lt;/script&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
